\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Teachable Humility (75):
\f0\b0  Your willingness to admit mistakes and invite dissent is your strongest asset. It acts as an emergency brake when you realize you've moved too fast or alienated someone.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Commitment to Fairness (68):
\f0\b0  A strong ethical baseline helps keep strategic impulses in check. You value integrity, which means you can recognize when standard influence crosses the line into unfair manipulation.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
